        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 187,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:38:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152992,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 187,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:38:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152993,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 187,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rete cystadenomas are typically unilateral with a hilar location but may uncommonly be bilateral. They range in size (mean: 90&nbsp;mm) and may be unilocular or multilocular, with thin walls, smooth lining, and clear fluid {2852648; 15991159}. Rete adenomas are typically well-circumscribed white and spongy lesions centred in the ovarian hilum {2852648; 9416702}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:38:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152994,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 187,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rete cystadenomas are centred in the ovarian hilum and are characterized by dilated irregularly spaced crevices with an inner epithelial lining composed of flat to cuboidal cells with scant eosinophilic to clear (uncommon) cytoplasm and minimal nuclear stratification. Cilia are absent. Cytological atypia and mitoses are rare or absent {2852648; 9416702}. Hilar Leydig cells may form a band peripheral to the cyst wall. Rete ovarii can also be seen in the vicinity {3804558}. Rete adenomas are also centred in the ovarian hilum; they are well circumscribed and composed of closely packed small elongated to round and dilated tubules, some with focal, variably complex intraluminal papillae. The lining epithelial cells are cuboidal to slightly columnar, with scant eosinophilic to pale cytoplasm, and lack significant cytological atypia and mitotic activity. They may contain Leydig/luteinized cells within the scant intervening stroma {2852648; 9416702}. The immunophenotype of the lining cells has not been well studied, but the cells are positive with epithelial markers {9416702}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:38:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152995,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 187,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:38:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
